Laravel v5.1

Tagged caches don't fire the cache events listed here: http://laravel.com/docs/5.1/cache#cache-events

Non-tagged caches use the Repository class: https://github.com/laravel/framework/blob/5.1/src/Illuminate/Cache/Repository.php#L95-L108

```
    public function get($key, $default = null)
    {
        $value = $this->store->get($key);
        if (is_null($value)) {
            $this->fireCacheEvent('missed', [$key]);
            $value = value($default);
        } else {
            $this->fireCacheEvent('hit', [$key, $value]);
        }
        return $value;
    }
```

Tagged caches extend from the TaggedCache class: https://github.com/laravel/framework/blob/5.1/src/Illuminate/Cache/TaggedCache.php#L57-L62

```
    public function get($key, $default = null)
    {
        $value = $this->store->get($this->taggedItemKey($key));
        return ! is_null($value) ? $value : value($default);
    }
```

I can have a go at adding it in and create a PR with these changes, if you'd like me to. I haven't yet as I saw https://github.com/laravel/framework/issues/9967 and figured that if it was being fixed then it this one can possibly be fixed at the same time. :-)

